I record the answer verbatim with its date in the backlog, republish, and act on it.

## Why

- **Stage 0 is not mine to shrink.** Today's ruling has every task brainstormed at backlog entry, whatever its size. No executor may exist before both product advisors confirm the joint doc and the voters approve it 2/2, so the 30-second tab changes nothing.
- **"Today" and "before 11:00" are wishes.** They decide no ballot and waive no gate. A brainstorm has no time box, so a deadline it cannot meet is a change of course, which is the operator's. That means one poll, recommendation first, naming the rule.
- **I neither obey nor overrule silently.** I start no executor. Round 1 starts now because it is the standing default, touches nothing live, and costs two discarded drafts if the operator waives.
- **My five-line idea stays out of the briefs.** I do not design, and a hint would turn two independent drafts into edits of my sketch.
- **Background calls** keep my session free for the poll.
- **The status claims nothing:** both tabs are still running and nothing live changed.
